"""
Tableau Prep Script: per-post risk-band roll-up of the Embassy Threat
Join's event-level pairs.

Generated by tableau-prep-etl skill from
templates/embassy_risk_summary.py.j2.

Sibling of `embassy_threat_join`: consumes the same upstream tail as
the join (the post×event-pair dataframe), aggregates to one row per
post over the configured rolling window, and assigns a final
risk_band suitable for a physical-security operations dashboard.

Banding rules (in priority order). Thresholds calibrated against
observed GDELT 7-day weighted-volume distribution across the curated
60-post roster — GDELT's event-row inflation (one row per source URL,
not one row per real-world event) means a single capital city's
ordinary news week produces dozens of weighted-event-points before
adjusting for severity.

  CRITICAL   weighted_threat_score >= 500  OR  any mass-violence event
             within 30mi within 72h
  HIGH       weighted_threat_score 150-499
  ELEVATED   weighted_threat_score 30-149
  GUARDED    weighted_threat_score 1-29
  LOW        weighted_threat_score 0  (default; includes posts with no
             events in window)

The recency-decay weighting lets a 24h-old assault outrank a 5-day-old
protest even when both are within range. Recency_score is on the
event-level table; we re-derive the days-old delta here so the summary
matches the dashboard's "as of now" view.
"""
